                <pb facs="0497" n="379" sameAs="frus:frus1929v03/pg379"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00Sonora/489: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul at Nogales</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Damm</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-04-02T18:00:00-05:00">April 2, 1929—6
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Press despatches of today from Naco report that Mexican rebel airplane this
                    morning bombed Naco, Arizona causing injury to American citizen. Telegraph facts
                    immediately to reach Department not later than nine o’clock Wednesday morning.
                    Similar telegram sent to Agua Prieta.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
